@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "zendesk.api"

Feature: Priority Routing
	Testing the routing of specific tickets to various priority levels

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I teardown the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown users with the following userExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| User1 |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Organization1 |

Scenario: Urgent Priority Routing
	End users who create requests for the Liferay DXP Cloud product with the system status as Production: Completely shut down should have their requests listed as priority level Urgent.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved            |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1 |
	| Tags             | liferay_dxp_cloud   |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                |
	| Shared Comments  | true                |
	| SLA              | Gold                |
	| Tier             | Regular             |
	| Support Region   | US                  |
	| Support Language | English             | 
	| External ID      | Organization1       |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | Portuguese                       |
	| Time Zone        | Brasilia                         | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	When I create several requests as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following product, component, and system status values
	| prd_liferay_dxp_cloud | backup_recovery     | production_completely_shutdown |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_cloud | connectivity        | production_completely_shutdown |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_cloud | networking          | production_completely_shutdown |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_cloud | system_availability | production_completely_shutdown |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_cloud | vpn                 | production_completely_shutdown |
	Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should be given the priority level "urgent"

Scenario: High Priority Routing DXP Cloud
	End users who create requests for the Liferay DXP Cloud product with the system status as Production: Severely impacted or inoperable should have their requests listed as priority level High.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved            |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1 |
	| Tags             | liferay_dxp_cloud   |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                |
	| Shared Comments  | true                |
	| SLA              | Gold                |
	| Tier             | Regular             |
	| Support Region   | US                  |
	| Support Language | English             | 
	| External ID      | Organization1       |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | Portuguese                       |
	| Time Zone        | Brasilia                         | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	When I create several requests as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following product, component, and system status values
	| prd_liferay_dxp_cloud | backup_recovery     | production_severely_impacted_inoperable |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_cloud | connectivity        | production_severely_impacted_inoperable |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_cloud | networking          | production_severely_impacted_inoperable |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_cloud | system_availability | production_severely_impacted_inoperable |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_cloud | vpn                 | production_severely_impacted_inoperable |
	Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should be given the priority level "high"

Scenario: High Priority Routing DXP
	End users who create requests for the Liferay DXP product with specific system statuses should have their requests listed as priority level High.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved            |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1 |
	| Tags             | liferay_dxp         |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                |
	| Shared Comments  | true                |
	| SLA              | Gold                |
	| Tier             | Regular             |
	| Support Region   | US                  |
	| Support Language | English             | 
	| External ID      | Organization1       |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | Portuguese                       |
	| Time Zone        | Brasilia                         | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	When I create several requests as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following product, component, and system status values
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_3 | apio_architect                | production_completely_shutdown          |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_2 | application_display_templates | production_severely_impacted_inoperable |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_1 | audience_targeting            | production_completely_shutdown          |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_0 | authentication                | production_severely_impacted_inoperable |
	Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should be given the priority level "high"

Scenario: Normal Priority Routing
	End users who create requests with specific system statuses should have their requests listed as priority level Normal.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved            |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1 |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                |
	| Shared Comments  | true                |
	| SLA              | Gold                |
	| Tier             | Regular             |
	| Support Region   | US                  |
	| Support Language | English             | 
	| External ID      | Organization1       |
	And I assign an organization with organizationExternalId "Organization1" with the following tags
	| developer_tools         |
	| enterprise_search       |
	| liferay_commerce        |
	| liferay_dxp             |
	| liferay_dxp_cloud       |
	| liferay_portal          |
	| management_tools_lcs    |
	| mobile_device_detection |
	| mobile_experience       |
	| productivity_tools_sync |
	| social_office           |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | Portuguese                       |
	| Time Zone        | Brasilia                         | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	When I create several requests as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following product, component, and system status values
	| prd_developer_tools         |                                        | production_unstable_with_periodic_interruptions      |
	| prd_enterprise_search       | monitoring                             | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities     |
	| prd_liferay_commerce_2_0    | apis_integrations_and_extension_points | production_fully_functional_with_observed_errors     |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_3         | apio_architect                         | non-production_completely_shutdown                   |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_2         | application_display_templates          | non-production_severely_impacted_inoperable          |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_cloud       | backup_recovery                        | non-production_unstable_with_periodic_interruptions  |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_2      | authentication                         | non-production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_1      | caching_clustering                     | production_unstable_with_periodic_interruptions      |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_0      | calendar                               | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities     |
	| prd_liferay_portal_5_2      | collaboration_suite                    | production_fully_functional_with_observed_errors     |
	| prd_management_tools_lcs    |                                        | non-production_completely_shutdown                   |
	| prd_mobile_device_detection |                                        | non-production_severely_impacted_inoperable          |
	| prd_mobile_experience       |                                        | non-production_unstable_with_periodic_interruptions  |
	| prd_productivity_tools_sync |                                        | non-production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| prd_social_office           |                                        | production_unstable_with_periodic_interruptions      |
	Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should be given the priority level "normal"

